 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for change delivery.** Fast updates without a realtime vendor justify owning connection capacity and reconnect operations. Five-second HTTPS polling is simpler and stateless but produces repeated reads and several seconds of lag; a hosted realtime service reduces connection operations but adds recurring fees and provider coupling. All three can meet the freshness target. See [Committed Change Delivery](decisions/change-delivery.md) for the comparison.
